---
// One picture for the "Works with the app closed" slideshow: the Word sidebar screenshot, how a browser save reaches the library
// (a diagram, not a screenshot), or an example agent chat over the core's MCP server: the question and answer are written for the
// page, the three tool calls and their results are real (run on a copy of the demo library). The chat plays message by message when
// its slide becomes active.
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
interface Props { id: "word" | "browser" | "agent" }
const { id } = Astro.props;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
{id === "word" && (
	<figure class="slide-shot">
		<img src={`${base}screenshots/word-sidebar.png`} width="1400" height="839" loading="lazy"
			alt="Word with the Zinc sidebar beside a paragraph with six numbered citations and a Vancouver bibliography; the sidebar shows the citation under the cursor" />
		<figcaption>The Word sidebar showing the citation under the cursor. Zinc is not running.</figcaption>
	</figure>
)}
{id === "browser" && (
	<figure class="slide-flow">
		<ol>
			<li><Icon name="globe" size={22} /><strong>A page in Chrome or Edge</strong><span>an article, a PDF, a search result</span></li>
			<li><Icon name="puzzle" size={22} /><strong>Zinc Connector</strong><span>click Save in the toolbar</span></li>
			<li><Icon name="terminal" size={22} /><strong>zotero-next-host.exe</strong><span>a small helper the browser starts</span></li>
			<li><Icon name="database" size={22} /><strong>Your library</strong><span>the item, its PDF and its collection</span></li>
		</ol>
		<p class="slide-off"><Icon name="power-off" size={14} />Zinc stays closed</p>
		<figcaption>How a save reaches your library without the app.</figcaption>
	</figure>
)}
{id === "agent" && (
	<figure class="slide-chat">
		<div class="chat" role="img" aria-label="An example chat: someone asks an agent for their deep learning papers; the agent searches the library, reads an item and returns a Vancouver reference list">
			<div class="chat-bar"><Icon name="bot" size={15} /><span>Agent</span><em>zotero-next MCP · your library</em></div>
			<div class="chat-body">
				<p class="msg msg-user" style="--i:0">Which papers in my library are about deep learning? Give me a Vancouver reference list.</p>
				<p class="msg msg-tool" style="--i:1"><Icon name="search" size={13} /><code>search_library</code> "deep learning" <span>→ 3 items</span></p>
				<p class="msg msg-tool" style="--i:2"><Icon name="file-text" size={13} /><code>get_item</code> ARTILGX9 <span>→ Nature 521(7553), DOI 10.1038/nature14539</span></p>
				<p class="msg msg-tool" style="--i:3"><Icon name="list-ordered" size={13} /><code>format_bibliography</code> vancouver <span>→ 3 references</span></p>
				<div class="msg msg-agent" style="--i:4">
					<p>You have three: LeCun et al. in <i>Nature</i> (2015), Gulshan et al. in <i>JAMA</i> (2016) and He et al. at CVPR (2016).</p>
					<ol>
						<li>LeCun Y, Bengio Y, Hinton G. Deep learning. Nature. 2015;521(7553):436–44.</li>
						<li>Gulshan V, Peng L, Coram M. Development and Validation of a Deep Learning Algorithm for Detection of Diabetic Retinopathy in Retinal Fundus Photographs. JAMA. 2016;316(22):2402–10.</li>
						<li>He K, Zhang X, Ren S, Sun J. Deep Residual Learning for Image Recognition. In: Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition. 2016. p. 770–8.</li>
					</ol>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<figcaption>An example chat. The tool calls and their results are real, run on the demo library; DOIs left out of the list for space.</figcaption>
	</figure>
)}
